From 2a2744265c58c098d11397632d8a234784a6f2fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ivines <aldemilopez@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 14:28:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Render before building the managers so RTX sensors have a
 frame

`_init_sim` calls `scene.update()` with the comment that it is "needed for the
observation manager to get valid tensors for initialization", but `scene.update()`
never renders. An RTX sensor has no frame until something renders, so the first
thing `ObservationManager._prepare_terms` does with an `image` term is ask a camera
for data that does not exist yet.

Without XR that resolves itself. With XR active it does not. The tiled camera blocks
forever in `isaac_rtx_renderer.render()` -> `wp.launch(reshape_tiled_image)`; with
GPU physics the same situation surfaces earlier as `CUDA error: an illegal memory
access was encountered` in `GpuArticulationView`. The non-tiled camera does not
block but returns an empty buffer, so the observation term is built with shape (0,)
and no image ever reaches the dataset. Either way, teleoperated recording with
cameras is impossible.

Scenes that load a large background USD happen to work, which is what made this look
like a scene-content problem for most of a day: the extra load time lets the renderer
produce a frame before anything asks for one. Ruled out by measurement on 2026-08-18,
all in the bare ground-plane-and-dome-light scene: hiding the ground grid, fixing the
ground material's missing textures, registering an empty background asset, adding
visible geometry in the camera's view, the dome light sampling strategy, the light
type, DLSS and rendermode, and pinning the robot root. None of them help; only
slow-loading assets do. That is a race, not a content requirement.

Four renders, only when RTX sensors are present, disabled with ARENA_PRERENDER=0.
RTX needs one warm-up frame anyway -- render 0 comes back black, render 1 has pixels.

With this, the bare scene records a demonstration whose camera stream is
(301, 480, 640, 3) with zero black frames.

Signed-off-by: ivines <aldemilopez@gmail.com>
---
 .../isaaclab/envs/manager_based_env.py        | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/isaaclab/isaaclab/envs/manager_based_env.py b/source/isaaclab/isaaclab/envs/manager_based_env.py
index 996e88216e..e7ed3e014f 100644
--- a/source/isaaclab/isaaclab/envs/manager_based_env.py
+++ b/source/isaaclab/isaaclab/envs/manager_based_env.py
@@ -195,6 +195,36 @@ class ManagerBasedEnv:
             # this shouldn't cause an issue since later on, users do a reset over all the environments
             # so the lazy buffers would be reset.
             self.scene.update(dt=self.physics_dt)
+
+            # LOCAL PATCH (2026-08-18): pump a few renders before the managers are built.
+            #
+            # The comment above says the scene update is "needed for the observation manager
+            # to get valid tensors for initialization", but `scene.update()` never renders.
+            # An RTX sensor has no frame until something renders, so the first thing
+            # `ObservationManager._prepare_terms` does with an `image` term is ask a camera
+            # for data that does not exist yet.
+            #
+            # Without XR that resolves itself. With XR active it does not: the tiled camera
+            # blocks forever in `isaac_rtx_renderer.render()` -> `wp.launch` (with GPU physics
+            # the same situation surfaces as `CUDA illegal memory access` in
+            # `GpuArticulationView`), and the non-tiled camera returns an empty buffer, so the
+            # observation term is built with shape (0,) and no image ever reaches the dataset.
+            #
+            # Scenes that load a large background USD happen to work, which is what made this
+            # look like a scene-content problem: the extra load time lets the renderer produce
+            # a frame before it is asked for. Measured on 2026-08-18: hiding the ground grid,
+            # registering an empty background, and adding visible geometry all fail to help --
+            # only slow-loading assets do. That is a race, not a content requirement.
+            #
+            # RTX also needs one warm-up frame: render 0 comes back black, render 1 has pixels.
+            # Set ARENA_PRERENDER=0 to disable this patch.
+            if bool(self.sim.get_setting("/isaaclab/render/rtx_sensors")):
+                import os as _os
+
+                _n = int(_os.environ.get("ARENA_PRERENDER", "4"))
+                for _ in range(_n):
+                    self.sim.render()
+
         # add timeline event to load managers
         self.load_managers()
 
